ring\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility\n*   **5. COVENANTS**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for distribution and payment.\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kWh.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The rate adjusted for inflation/escalation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made to the supplier for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.).\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and credits associated with renewable energy production.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kW.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A supplier meeting specific program requirements.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit for facility operations.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements including the *Electricity Act, 1998*.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legally binding assertions regarding the facility and supplier status.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises to maintain facility characteristics and notify of changes."} {:summary "### **Project Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **Section 5: [Continued from previous]**\n    *   **5.1.3**: Restrictions on increasing Nameplate Capacity (Max 10 kW).\n    *   **5.1.4**: Restrictions on modifying solar PV inverter/array ratings or facility character.\n*   **5.2: Metering**\n    *   **5.2.1**: Exclusivity of the meter to the Facility.\n    *   **5.2.2**: Ownership/operation of the meter by the Local Distribution Company (LDC).\n*   **5.3: Eligibility**\n    *   **5.3.1**: Requirement to maintain status as an \"Eligible Participant.\"\n*   **Section 6: GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1**: Access Rights (Inspection and Audit).\n    *   **6.2**: Electricity (Prohibition of substituted electricity sources).\n    *   **6.3**: Meter and Meter Data (Access and data release authorization).\n    *   **6.4**: Freedom of Information (FIPPA compliance).\n    *   **6.5**: Collection, Disclosure, and Consent of Information.\n    *   **6.6**: Statement Copies (Document production and verification).\n    *   **6.7**: Supplier Verification and Use of a Representative.\n*   **Section 7: NOTICES**\n    *   **7.1**: Address for Notice (OPA and Supplier email protocols).\n    *   **7.2**: Change of Contact Information (Prescribed Form requirement).\n    *   **7.3**: Timing of Notice (Deemed receipt rules).\n*   **Section 8: TERMINATION**\n    *   **8.1**: Termination on Notice (30 days by Supplier).\n    *   **8.2**: Termination for Breach (10 Business Days cure period).\n    *   **8.3**: Automatic Termination (Upon termination of Connection Agreement).\n*   **Section 9: AMENDMENT** (Requirement for written agreement in Prescribed Form).\n*   **Section 10: ASSIGNMENT** (Conditions for transferring rights).\n*   **Section 11: GOVERNING LAW** (Ontario and Canadian federal laws).\n*   **Section 12: DISPUTE RESOLUTION** (Good faith efforts and Arbitration).\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The maximum rated output of the facility (capped at 10 kW).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity owning the meter and managing local grid connection.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain to remain in the program.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The contracting authority (and its successors).\n*   **FIPPA:** *Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act*.\n*   **Prescribed Form:** Specific templates or formats required by the OPA for formal notifications/amendments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate required contract for grid synchronization; its termination triggers automatic contract termination.\n*   **Assignment:** The legal transfer of contract rights/obligations to a third party.\n*   **Arbitration:** The defined process for resolving disputes outside of court via an Arbitrator.\n*   **Business Day:** Defined for the purpose of identifying notice deadlines (cutoff 5:00 p.m.)."} {:summary "This section of the **microFIT Version 3.1.1** contract details dispute resolution mechanisms, payment guarantees, liability for multi-party suppliers, and the commencement of the definitions appendix.\n\n### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **[No Heading] (Dispute Resolution Continued)**\n    *   Unnumbered clauses addressing Arbitrator powers under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*, finality of decisions, and OPA’s right to consolidate similar supplier claims for efficiency.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY**\n    *   Addresses OPA’s guarantee of Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for suppliers not acting as a single legal entity.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a multi-person supplier.\n*   **APPENDIX A: DEFINITIONS**\n    *   Alphabetical list of defined terms used throughout the agreement.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal / Procedural Terms:**\n*   **Arbitration:** Process governed by the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*; seat is Toronto.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** Legal obligation where all parties in a group are individually and collectively responsible for the entire liability.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the prerequisite dispute resolution process.\n*   **Abut:** Technical definition regarding property boundaries and rights-of-way.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal classification based on Property Identification Numbers, the *Planning Act (Ontario)*, or Crown/Reserve land status.\n*   **Governmental Authority:** Includes federal, provincial, or municipal bodies (e.g., Ontario Energy Board, Electrical Safety Authority).\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, bylaws, common law, and the Retail Settlement Code.\n\n**Financial / Technical Terms:**\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The primary contracting party and guarantor.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for making payments to the supplier in the first instance.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments payable to the Supplier under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Contract Price:** The per kWh price determined by the **FIT Price Schedule** and the **Base Date**.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Ontario-specific index used for economic adjustments.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights to renewable energy certificates, carbon offsets, and emission reduction allowances.\n*   **Directly vs. Indirectly Connected Facility:** Classification based on whether the facility's connection is independent of or associated with a load customer."} {:summary "### **Section Headings and Annexes**\n*   **Appendix A (Continued):** (Concluding definitions from the previous section).\n*   **Appendix B:** CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE.\n*   **Appendix C:** SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-1:** DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-2:** INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix E:** LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE.\n\n### **Clause Numbers**\n*   **Appendix D-1:**\n    *   1. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clause 1.1)\n    *   2. COVENANTS (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **Appendix D-2:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. PERMITTED BATTERY BACK-UP CONFIGURATION\n*   **Appendix E:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   3. ADDITIONAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS (Clauses 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The electricity distributor named in the contract.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The rated capacity of the facility (max 10 kW).\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the Contract Price subject to CPI-based increases.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including renewable fuel type, Ontario location, and metering standards.\n*   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, or waterpower.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price (CPy):** The price adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI).\n*   **Rooftop Facility:** A solar project integrated into an existing building structure.\n*   **In Parallel:** A metering configuration where the facility is between the load customer and the distribution system.\n*   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Legal status of land use (e.g., residential vs. agricultural).\n*   **IESO (Independent Electricity System Operator):** The entity governing the Ontario electricity market.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, by-laws, IESO market rules, and OEB codes.\n*   **Commercial Operation:** The milestone marking the official start of energy production for the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations for the Supplier, particularly regarding battery configurations and connection types."} {:summary "**Sections and Clause Numbers:**\n*   **3.5**: Data release and third-party authorization requirements.\n*   **3.6**: Records retention, settlement statements, and exclusion of General Terms and Conditions.\n\n**Key Legal and Financial Terms:**\n*   **Advanced Notice**: A requirement for the OPA to provide at least two days' notice for meter access.\n*   **Irrevocably Authorize**: A legal requirement for the Supplier to give permanent permission to third parties/agencies to share data with the OPA.\n*   **Administering the Contract**: The defined purpose for which data and information may be requested or shared.\n*   **Settlement Statements**: Financial documents detailing the calculation of payments for electricity generated.\n*   **Generation Payment**: The financial compensation paid to the Supplier for electricity produced by the Facility.\n*   **Section 6.6 of Part 2**: A specific provision of the general contract terms that is explicitly declared not to apply to this agreement."}]}, :node-id #uuid "c7972d77-97bf-4dd2-841f-fefd2902b741", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225", :event/id #uuid "019e4327-546e-70af-844e-3922862ca8f6"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi-Fgf3clHlABItbdOhlJ8cm6R0y", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111534, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi-Fgf3clHlABItbdOhlJ8cm6R0y", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
