e for distribution and payment.\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kWh.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The rate adjusted for inflation/escalation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made to the supplier for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.).\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and credits associated with renewable energy production.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kW.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A supplier meeting specific program requirements.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit for facility operations.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements including the *Electricity Act, 1998*.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legally binding assertions regarding the facility and supplier status.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises to maintain facility characteristics and notify of changes." "### **Project Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **Section 5: [Continued from previous]**\n    *   **5.1.3**: Restrictions on increasing Nameplate Capacity (Max 10 kW).\n    *   **5.1.4**: Restrictions on modifying solar PV inverter/array ratings or facility character.\n*   **5.2: Metering**\n    *   **5.2.1**: Exclusivity of the meter to the Facility.\n    *   **5.2.2**: Ownership/operation of the meter by the Local Distribution Company (LDC).\n*   **5.3: Eligibility**\n    *   **5.3.1**: Requirement to maintain status as an \"Eligible Participant.\"\n*   **Section 6: GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1**: Access Rights (Inspection and Audit).\n    *   **6.2**: Electricity (Prohibition of substituted electricity sources).\n    *   **6.3**: Meter and Meter Data (Access and data release authorization).\n    *   **6.4**: Freedom of Information (FIPPA compliance).\n    *   **6.5**: Collection, Disclosure, and Consent of Information.\n    *   **6.6**: Statement Copies (Document production and verification).\n    *   **6.7**: Supplier Verification and Use of a Representative.\n*   **Section 7: NOTICES**\n    *   **7.1**: Address for Notice (OPA and Supplier email protocols).\n    *   **7.2**: Change of Contact Information (Prescribed Form requirement).\n    *   **7.3**: Timing of Notice (Deemed receipt rules).\n*   **Section 8: TERMINATION**\n    *   **8.1**: Termination on Notice (30 days by Supplier).\n    *   **8.2**: Termination for Breach (10 Business Days cure period).\n    *   **8.3**: Automatic Termination (Upon termination of Connection Agreement).\n*   **Section 9: AMENDMENT** (Requirement for written agreement in Prescribed Form).\n*   **Section 10: ASSIGNMENT** (Conditions for transferring rights).\n*   **Section 11: GOVERNING LAW** (Ontario and Canadian federal laws).\n*   **Section 12: DISPUTE RESOLUTION** (Good faith efforts and Arbitration).\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The maximum rated output of the facility (capped at 10 kW).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity owning the meter and managing local grid connection.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain to remain in the program.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The contracting authority (and its successors).\n*   **FIPPA:** *Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act*.\n*   **Prescribed Form:** Specific templates or formats required by the OPA for formal notifications/amendments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate required contract for grid synchronization; its termination triggers automatic contract termination.\n*   **Assignment:** The legal transfer of contract rights/obligations to a third party.\n*   **Arbitration:** The defined process for resolving disputes outside of court via an Arbitrator.\n*   **Business Day:** Defined for the purpose of identifying notice deadlines (cutoff 5:00 p.m.)." "This section of the **microFIT Version 3.1.1** contract details dispute resolution mechanisms, payment guarantees, liability for multi-party suppliers, and the commencement of the definitions appendix.\n\n### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **[No Heading] (Dispute Resolution Continued)**\n    *   Unnumbered clauses addressing Arbitrator powers under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*, finality of decisions, and OPA’s right to consolidate similar supplier claims for efficiency.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY**\n    *   Addresses OPA’s guarantee of Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for suppliers not acting as a single legal entity.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a multi-person supplier.\n*   **APPENDIX A: DEFINITIONS**\n    *   Alphabetical list of defined terms used throughout the agreement.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal / Procedural Terms:**\n*   **Arbitration:** Process governed by the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*; seat is Toronto.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** Legal obligation where all parties in a group are individually and collectively responsible for the entire liability.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the prerequisite dispute resolution process.\n*   **Abut:** Technical definition regarding property boundaries and rights-of-way.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal classification based on Property Identification Numbers, the *Planning Act (Ontario)*, or Crown/Reserve land status.\n*   **Governmental Authority:** Includes federal, provincial, or municipal bodies (e.g., Ontario Energy Board, Electrical Safety Authority).\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, bylaws, common law, and the Retail Settlement Code.\n\n**Financial / Technical Terms:**\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The primary contracting party and guarantor.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for making payments to the supplier in the first instance.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments payable to the Supplier under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Contract Price:** The per kWh price determined by the **FIT Price Schedule** and the **Base Date**.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Ontario-specific index used for economic adjustments.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights to renewable energy certificates, carbon offsets, and emission reduction allowances.\n*   **Directly vs. Indirectly Connected Facility:** Classification based on whether the facility's connection is independent of or associated with a load customer." "### **Section Headings and Annexes**\n*   **Appendix A (Continued):** (Concluding definitions from the previous section).\n*   **Appendix B:** CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE.\n*   **Appendix C:** SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-1:** DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-2:** INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix E:** LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE.\n\n### **Clause Numbers**\n*   **Appendix D-1:**\n    *   1. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clause 1.1)\n    *   2. COVENANTS (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **Appendix D-2:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. PERMITTED BATTERY BACK-UP CONFIGURATION\n*   **Appendix E:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   3. ADDITIONAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS (Clauses 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The electricity distributor named in the contract.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The rated capacity of the facility (max 10 kW).\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the Contract Price subject to CPI-based increases.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including renewable fuel type, Ontario location, and metering standards.\n*   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, or waterpower.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price (CPy):** The price adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI).\n*   **Rooftop Facility:** A solar project integrated into an existing building structure.\n*   **In Parallel:** A metering configuration where the facility is between the load customer and the distribution system.\n*   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Legal status of land use (e.g., residential vs. agricultural).\n*   **IESO (Independent Electricity System Operator):** The entity governing the Ontario electricity market.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, by-laws, IESO market rules, and OEB codes.\n*   **Commercial Operation:** The milestone marking the official start of energy production for the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations for the Supplier, particularly regarding battery configurations and connection types." "**Sections and Clause Numbers:**\n*   **3.5**: Data release and third-party authorization requirements.\n*   **3.6**: Records retention, settlement statements, and exclusion of General Terms and Conditions.\n\n**Key Legal and Financial Terms:**\n*   **Advanced Notice**: A requirement for the OPA to provide at least two days' notice for meter access.\n*   **Irrevocably Authorize**: A legal requirement for the Supplier to give permanent permission to third parties/agencies to share data with the OPA.\n*   **Administering the Contract**: The defined purpose for which data and information may be requested or shared.\n*   **Settlement Statements**: Financial documents detailing the calculation of payments for electricity generated.\n*   **Generation Payment**: The financial compensation paid to the Supplier for electricity produced by the Facility.\n*   **Section 6.6 of Part 2**: A specific provision of the general contract terms that is explicitly declared not to apply to this agreement."]}}, :duration-ms 1, :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225"] [:node #uuid "c7972d77-97bf-4dd2-841f-fefd2902b741"] [:tick #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:11:51.541396-05:00", :status :success, :node-id #uuid "c7972d77-97bf-4dd2-841f-fefd2902b741", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-completed, :sheet-id #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225", :event/id #uuid "019e4327-5475-7058-a9e5-2f27ee8083f2"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi160SzkuPGWV-cQC_ujrmFwFdgD", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111542, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi160SzkuPGWV-cQC_ujrmFwFdgD", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1y6f1gzO2HL7Xs2Fi9jnkcVzAt", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1y6f1gzO2HL7Xs2Fi9jnkcVzAt", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi28sq80G-M3kWFW399N-EGi7l2J", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111547, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 774208, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717", :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225"] [:tick #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717"] [:node #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:11:51.545818-05:00", :inputs {:v2_full_map {:summary ["### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. Contract and Supplier Information**: Clauses (1) through (11).\n*   **B. Facility Characteristics**: Clauses (1) through (8).\n*   **C. Documents Included; Defined Terms**: Unnumbered list of Appendices (A through E).\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. Term**\n*   **2. Pricing Provisions and Payment**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price (2.1.1, 2.1.2)\n    *   2.2. Payment (2.2.1, 2.2.2)\n*   **3. Environmental Attributes**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. Representations and Warranties**\n    *   4.1. Connection (4.1.1–4.1.3)\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics (4.2.1–4.2.3)\n    *   4.3. Metering (4.3.1–4.3.3)\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance (4.4.1–4.4.6)\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility (4.5.1–4.5.3)\n*   **5. Covenants**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics (5.1.1)\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal Terms**\n*   **Ontario Power Authority (OPA):** The contracting entity/procurer.\n*   **Supplier:** The legal entity/individual constructing and operating the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and payments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** The Micro-Embedded Generation Facility Connection Agreement.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements the Supplier must follow.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights, titles, and interests associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **Regulatory Environmental Attributes:** Attributes created/allocated under Laws and Regulations.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit (if applicable).\n*   **Eligible Participant:** Specific status required for Supplier eligibility as defined in the rules.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legal assurances provided by the Supplier to the OPA regarding facts and compliance.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises made by the Supplier for the duration of the contract term.\n\n**Financial Terms**\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kilowatt-hour ($/kWh).\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price taking into account escalation factors.\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the price subject to indexation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made by the LDC for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The periodic billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.) for payments.\n*   **Base Date:** The reference date used for price calculations.\n*   **Domestic Content Level:** Requirement for a minimum percentage (60% for solar PV) of local sourcing for equipment.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kilowatts (kW)." "### **Legal and Financial Summary: microFIT Contract Version 2.0**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **5.1. (Continued):** Specific Covenants (Clauses 5.1.2 – 5.1.4)\n*   **5.2. Metering:** (Clauses 5.2.1 – 5.2.2)\n*   **5.3. Eligibility:** (Clause 5.3.1)\n*   **6. GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1. Access Rights**\n    *   **6.2. Electricity**\n    *   **6.3. Meter and Meter Data:** (Clauses 6.3.1 – 6.3.2)\n    *   **6.4. Freedom of Information**\n    *   **6.5. Collection of Information** (Includes sub-headers: *Disclosure of Information* and *Consent*)\n    *   **6.6. Statement Copies**\n    *   **6.7. Supplier Verification and use of a Representative**\n*   **7. NOTICES:** (Clauses 7.1 – 7.3)\n*   **8. TERMINATION:** (Clauses 8.1 – 8.3)\n*   **9. AMENDMENT**\n*   **10. ASSIGNMENT**\n*   **11. GOVERNING LAW**\n*   **12. DISPUTE RESOLUTION**\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain \"at all times\" to remain in the program.\n*   **FIPPA (Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act):** Acknowledges that the OPA is subject to public disclosure laws regarding the data held.\n*   **Irrevocable Authorization:** The Supplier’s permanent grant of permission to the LDC to release facility data to the OPA.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate contract; its termination results in the **Automatic Termination** of the microFIT contract (Clause 8.3).\n*   **Assignment:** The transfer of rights/obligations. Allowed only in total (not partial) to another Eligible Participant, subject to OPA consent.\n*   **Governing Law:** The laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada.\n*   **Arbitration:** A voluntary alternative dispute resolution mechanism if amicable good faith efforts fail after 90 days.\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Technical Terms**\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to a maximum of **10 kW**; modification to increase this is prohibited (Clause 5.1.3).\n*   **Inverter Rating / Solar Array Rating:** Technical specifications from Part 1 that the Supplier is barred from modifying (Clause 5.1.4).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity that must own and operate the Facility’s meter.\n*   **Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** Data required to ensure the facility meets Ontario-sourced equipment requirements.\n*   **Reference Number:** The unique identifier required for all formal e-mail communications with the OPA.\n*   **Generation Payment:** Financial payments for electricity; OPA has the right to audit settlement statements and invoices to verify accuracy." "### Section Headings and Clause Numbers\n*   **[Unnamed Section] (Continuation of Dispute Resolution):** Found on Page 10, covering arbitration procedures and OPA's right to consolidate similar claims.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY:** Outlines OPA guarantees regarding Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES:**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for multi-entity suppliers.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a supplier group.\n*   **APPENDIX A - DEFINITIONS:** Provides legal and technical meanings for specific terms used throughout the contract.\n\n### Key Legal and Financial Terms\n*   **Arbitrator:** An official from the Superior Court of Justice (Toronto Region) empowered under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)* to deliver final and binding decisions.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** A legal obligation where all parties in a group are collectively and individually responsible for the entire liability or obligation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments guaranteed by the OPA if the Local Distribution Company (LDC) fails to pay under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Abut:** Specifically defined property boundaries sharing a common border or separated by a right-of-way of 15 metres or less.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal definition used to group land parcels based on Property Identification Numbers (PINs) or ownership for program eligibility.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and interests (credits, offsets, certificates) associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and initial payment to the supplier.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The central counterparty to the contract.\n*   **Retail Settlement Code / Distribution System Code:** Regulatory frameworks established by the Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** The financial index used for potential price adjustments, established by Statistics Canada.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the standard arbitration prerequisite." "### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Definitions (Unlabeled Section, Pages 14-15):** Includes definitions from \"LDC\" through \"Term.\"\n*   **APPENDIX B: CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE (Page 16):**\n    *   Clauses (a) and (b) regarding Indexed Pricing Periods.\n*   **APPENDIX C: SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE (Pages 17-18):**\n    *   **ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS:** Definitions for \"Existing Building\" and \"Rooftop Facility.\"\n    *   **DOMESTIC CONTENT REQUIREMENTS:** Clauses 1.1 through 1.7.\n    *   **Table 1:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Crystalline Silicon PV Technology.\n    *   **Table 2:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Thin-Film PV Technology.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **Financial/Pricing Terms:**\n    *   **Contract Price:** The base price for electricity.\n    *   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price based on CPI.\n    *   **Percentage Escalated (PE):** The portion of the price subject to inflation adjustments.\n    *   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Used for calculating price escalation.\n    *   **Settlement Price/Settlement Period:** Terms governing the payment and accounting for electricity sales.\n*   **Technical/Regulatory Terms:**\n    *   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to 10 kW for microFIT eligibility.\n    *   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including location (Ontario), fuel type, and connection to the IESO Controlled Grid.\n    *   **Domestic Content Level/Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** The percentage of equipment/services that must originate in Ontario.\n    *   **Designated Activities:** Specific manufacturing or service tasks that earn \"Qualifying Percentages\" toward domestic content targets.\n    *   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, and waterpower.\n    *   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for local electricity delivery.\n    *   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Regulatory permit from the Ministry of the Environment.\n    *   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Zoning/legal status of the property (Residential, Agricultural, Commercial, Industrial).\n    *   **Property Identification Number (PIN):** Legal identifier for land parcels." "### **Legal and Financial Analysis: microFIT Version 2.0 (Page 19-23)**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Table 3: Domestic Content Grid** – Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Concentrated PV Technology.\n*   **APPENDIX D -1: DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clause 1.1)\n    *   Clause 2: Covenants (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **APPENDIX D -2: INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Permitted Battery Back-up Configuration\n*   **APPENDIX E: LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   Clause 3: Additional Terms and Conditions (Sub-clauses 3.1 through 3.6)\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Explicit assertions made by the Supplier (e.g., regarding battery backup and distributor status) upon which the OPA (Ontario Power Authority) relies to enter the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises the Supplier must fulfill throughout the Term of the contract.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** A broad definition including federal/provincial statutes, IESO Market Rules, and OEB (Ontario Energy Board) codes.\n*   **Force Majeure/Disconnection:** Provision 3.3 defines a \"deemed permanent disconnection\" if a facility is offline for more than 20 continuous Business Days.\n*   **Information Rights/Access:** The OPA is granted irrevocable authorization to access meter data and third-party information (Clauses 3.4, 3.5).\n*   **Resident in Ontario:** A qualifying criterion for labor and services to meet domestic content requirements.\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Operational Terms**\n*   **Designated Activity / Qualifying Percentage:** These define the \"Domestic Content\" requirements. For Concentrated PV, items like cells (14%), primary optics (9%), and labor (19%) contribute to a mandatory 100% total.\n*   **Ontario Supplier:** A vendor required for qualifying electrical hardware (5%–9% toward domestic content).\n*   **Generation Payments:** Financial settlements for power produced, specifically handled through the IESO for LDC Suppliers (Clause 3.2).\n*   **In Parallel:** A specific technical/metering configuration defining the relationship between the facility, the load customer, and the distribution system.\n\n#### **4. Referenced Regulatory Bodies/Codes**\n*   **OPA:** Ontario Power Authority.\n*   **IESO:** Independent Electricity System Operator.\n*   **OEB:** Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **Applicable Codes:** Electricity Act 1998, Transmission System Code, Distribution System Code, Retail Settlement Code."]}, :v3_full_map {:summary ["### **Section Headings and Clauses**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. CONTRACT AND SUPPLIER INFORMATION**\n    *   (1) Reference Number\n    *   (2) Supplier Name\n    *   (3) Contract Commencement Date\n    *   (4) Contract End Date\n    *   (5) Legal Entity Relationship to LDC (Connection Agreement)\n    *   (6) LDC Generator Account Number\n    *   (7) Contract Price\n    *   (8) Percentage Escalated\n    *   (9) Base Date\n    *   (10) Supplier Contact Information\n    *   (11) Representative Contact Information\n*   **B. FACILITY CHARACTERISTICS**\n    *   (1) LDC Distribution System Connection\n    *   (2) Facility Location (PIN and Address)\n    *   (3) Renewable Fuel type\n    *   (4) Nameplate Capacity (kW)\n    *   (5) Solar PV Specifics (Inverter/Array ratings, Rooftop status)\n    *   (6) Connection type (Directly/Indirectly/In Parallel)\n    *   (7) Battery Back-up compliance\n    *   (8) Wind Capacity specifics\n*   **C. DOCUMENTS INCLUDED; DEFINED TERMS**\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. TERM**\n*   **2. PRICING PROVISIONS AND PAYMENT**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price\n    *   2.2. Payment (Generation Payments, Settlement Period)\n*   **3. ENVIRONMENTAL ATTRIBUTES**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register (Regulatory Environmental Attributes)\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES**\n    *   4.1. Connection\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics\n    *   4.3. Metering\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility\n*   **5. COVENANTS**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for distribution and payment.\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kWh.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The rate adjusted for inflation/escalation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made to the supplier for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.).\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and credits associated with renewable energy production.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kW.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A supplier meeting specific program requirements.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit for facility operations.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements including the *Electricity Act, 1998*.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legally binding assertions regarding the facility and supplier status.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises to maintain facility characteristics and notify of changes." "### **Project Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **Section 5: [Continued from previous]**\n    *   **5.1.3**: Restrictions on increasing Nameplate Capacity (Max 10 kW).\n    *   **5.1.4**: Restrictions on modifying solar PV inverter/array ratings or facility character.\n*   **5.2: Metering**\n    *   **5.2.1**: Exclusivity of the meter to the Facility.\n    *   **5.2.2**: Ownership/operation of the meter by the Local Distribution Company (LDC).\n*   **5.3: Eligibility**\n    *   **5.3.1**: Requirement to maintain status as an \"Eligible Participant.\"\n*   **Section 6: GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1**: Access Rights (Inspection and Audit).\n    *   **6.2**: Electricity (Prohibition of substituted electricity sources).\n    *   **6.3**: Meter and Meter Data (Access and data release authorization).\n    *   **6.4**: Freedom of Information (FIPPA compliance).\n    *   **6.5**: Collection, Disclosure, and Consent of Information.\n    *   **6.6**: Statement Copies (Document production and verification).\n    *   **6.7**: Supplier Verification and Use of a Representative.\n*   **Section 7: NOTICES**\n    *   **7.1**: Address for Notice (OPA and Supplier email protocols).\n    *   **7.2**: Change of Contact Information (Prescribed Form requirement).\n    *   **7.3**: Timing of Notice (Deemed receipt rules).\n*   **Section 8: TERMINATION**\n    *   **8.1**: Termination on Notice (30 days by Supplier).\n    *   **8.2**: Termination for Breach (10 Business Days cure period).\n    *   **8.3**: Automatic Termination (Upon termination of Connection Agreement).\n*   **Section 9: AMENDMENT** (Requirement for written agreement in Prescribed Form).\n*   **Section 10: ASSIGNMENT** (Conditions for transferring rights).\n*   **Section 11: GOVERNING LAW** (Ontario and Canadian federal laws).\n*   **Section 12: DISPUTE RESOLUTION** (Good faith efforts and Arbitration).\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The maximum rated output of the facility (capped at 10 kW).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity owning the meter and managing local grid connection.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain to remain in the program.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The contracting authority (and its successors).\n*   **FIPPA:** *Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act*.\n*   **Prescribed Form:** Specific templates or formats required by the OPA for formal notifications/amendments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate required contract for grid synchronization; its termination triggers automatic contract termination.\n*   **Assignment:** The legal transfer of contract rights/obligations to a third party.\n*   **Arbitration:** The defined process for resolving disputes outside of court via an Arbitrator.\n*   **Business Day:** Defined for the purpose of identifying notice deadlines (cutoff 5:00 p.m.)." "This section of the **microFIT Version 3.1.1** contract details dispute resolution mechanisms, payment guarantees, liability for multi-party suppliers, and the commencement of the definitions appendix.\n\n### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **[No Heading] (Dispute Resolution Continued)**\n    *   Unnumbered clauses addressing Arbitrator powers under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*, finality of decisions, and OPA’s right to consolidate similar supplier claims for efficiency.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY**\n    *   Addresses OPA’s guarantee of Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for suppliers not acting as a single legal entity.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a multi-person supplier.\n*   **APPENDIX A: DEFINITIONS**\n    *   Alphabetical list of defined terms used throughout the agreement.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal / Procedural Terms:**\n*   **Arbitration:** Process governed by the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*; seat is Toronto.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** Legal obligation where all parties in a group are individually and collectively responsible for the entire liability.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the prerequisite dispute resolution process.\n*   **Abut:** Technical definition regarding property boundaries and rights-of-way.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal classification based on Property Identification Numbers, the *Planning Act (Ontario)*, or Crown/Reserve land status.\n*   **Governmental Authority:** Includes federal, provincial, or municipal bodies (e.g., Ontario Energy Board, Electrical Safety Authority).\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, bylaws, common law, and the Retail Settlement Code.\n\n**Financial / Technical Terms:**\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The primary contracting party and guarantor.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for making payments to the supplier in the first instance.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments payable to the Supplier under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Contract Price:** The per kWh price determined by the **FIT Price Schedule** and the **Base Date**.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Ontario-specific index used for economic adjustments.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights to renewable energy certificates, carbon offsets, and emission reduction allowances.\n*   **Directly vs. Indirectly Connected Facility:** Classification based on whether the facility's connection is independent of or associated with a load customer." "### **Section Headings and Annexes**\n*   **Appendix A (Continued):** (Concluding definitions from the previous section).\n*   **Appendix B:** CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE.\n*   **Appendix C:** SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-1:** DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-2:** INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix E:** LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE.\n\n### **Clause Numbers**\n*   **Appendix D-1:**\n    *   1. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clause 1.1)\n    *   2. COVENANTS (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **Appendix D-2:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. PERMITTED BATTERY BACK-UP CONFIGURATION\n*   **Appendix E:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   3. ADDITIONAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS (Clauses 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The electricity distributor named in the contract.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The rated capacity of the facility (max 10 kW).\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the Contract Price subject to CPI-based increases.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including renewable fuel type, Ontario location, and metering standards.\n*   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, or waterpower.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price (CPy):** The price adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI).\n*   **Rooftop Facility:** A solar project integrated into an existing building structure.\n*   **In Parallel:** A metering configuration where the facility is between the load customer and the distribution system.\n*   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Legal status of land use (e.g., residential vs. agricultural).\n*   **IESO (Independent Electricity System Operator):** The entity governing the Ontario electricity market.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, by-laws, IESO market rules, and OEB codes.\n*   **Commercial Operation:** The milestone marking the official start of energy production for the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations for the Supplier, particularly regarding battery configurations and connection types." "**Sections and Clause Numbers:**\n*   **3.5**: Data release and third-party authorization requirements.\n*   **3.6**: Records retention, settlement statements, and exclusion of General Terms and Conditions.\n\n**Key Legal and Financial Terms:**\n*   **Advanced Notice**: A requirement for the OPA to provide at least two days' notice for meter access.\n*   **Irrevocably Authorize**: A legal requirement for the Supplier to give permanent permission to third parties/agencies to share data with the OPA.\n*   **Administering the Contract**: The defined purpose for which data and information may be requested or shared.\n*   **Settlement Statements**: Financial documents detailing the calculation of payments for electricity generated.\n*   **Generation Payment**: The financial compensation paid to the Supplier for electricity produced by the Facility.\n*   **Section 6.6 of Part 2**: A specific provision of the general contract terms that is explicitly declared not to apply to this agreement."]}}, :node-id #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225", :event/id #uuid "019e4327-5479-702d-b4f2-fe43c9220df3"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1y6f1gzO2HL7Xs2Fi9jnkcVzAt", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111546, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1y6f1gzO2HL7Xs2Fi9jnkcVzAt", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xxu1xJ-gxmnzNU1owhfFAOkOX", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xxu1xJ-gxmnzNU1owhfFAOkOX", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi2BnEpYWO8VK7lQx0eKHi3OWyww", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111547, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 974541, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717", :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225"] [:tick #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717"] [:node #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:11:51.545818-05:00", :inputs {:v2_full_map {:summary ["### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. Contract and Supplier Information**: Clauses (1) through (11).\n*   **B. Facility Characteristics**: Clauses (1) through (8).\n*   **C. Documents Included; Defined Terms**: Unnumbered list of Appendices (A through E).\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. Term**\n*   **2. Pricing Provisions and Payment**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price (2.1.1, 2.1.2)\n    *   2.2. Payment (2.2.1, 2.2.2)\n*   **3. Environmental Attributes**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. Representations and Warranties**\n    *   4.1. Connection (4.1.1–4.1.3)\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics (4.2.1–4.2.3)\n    *   4.3. Metering (4.3.1–4.3.3)\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance (4.4.1–4.4.6)\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility (4.5.1–4.5.3)\n*   **5. Covenants**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics (5.1.1)\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal Terms**\n*   **Ontario Power Authority (OPA):** The contracting entity/procurer.\n*   **Supplier:** The legal entity/individual constructing and operating the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and payments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** The Micro-Embedded Generation Facility Connection Agreement.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements the Supplier must follow.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights, titles, and interests associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **Regulatory Environmental Attributes:** Attributes created/allocated under Laws and Regulations.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit (if applicable).\n*   **Eligible Participant:** Specific status required for Supplier eligibility as defined in the rules.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legal assurances provided by the Supplier to the OPA regarding facts and compliance.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises made by the Supplier for the duration of the contract term.\n\n**Financial Terms**\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kilowatt-hour ($/kWh).\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price taking into account escalation factors.\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the price subject to indexation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made by the LDC for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The periodic billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.) for payments.\n*   **Base Date:** The reference date used for price calculations.\n*   **Domestic Content Level:** Requirement for a minimum percentage (60% for solar PV) of local sourcing for equipment.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kilowatts (kW)." "### **Legal and Financial Summary: microFIT Contract Version 2.0**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **5.1. (Continued):** Specific Covenants (Clauses 5.1.2 – 5.1.4)\n*   **5.2. Metering:** (Clauses 5.2.1 – 5.2.2)\n*   **5.3. Eligibility:** (Clause 5.3.1)\n*   **6. GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1. Access Rights**\n    *   **6.2. Electricity**\n    *   **6.3. Meter and Meter Data:** (Clauses 6.3.1 – 6.3.2)\n    *   **6.4. Freedom of Information**\n    *   **6.5. Collection of Information** (Includes sub-headers: *Disclosure of Information* and *Consent*)\n    *   **6.6. Statement Copies**\n    *   **6.7. Supplier Verification and use of a Representative**\n*   **7. NOTICES:** (Clauses 7.1 – 7.3)\n*   **8. TERMINATION:** (Clauses 8.1 – 8.3)\n*   **9. AMENDMENT**\n*   **10. ASSIGNMENT**\n*   **11. GOVERNING LAW**\n*   **12. DISPUTE RESOLUTION**\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain \"at all times\" to remain in the program.\n*   **FIPPA (Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act):** Acknowledges that the OPA is subject to public disclosure laws regarding the data held.\n*   **Irrevocable Authorization:** The Supplier’s permanent grant of permission to the LDC to release facility data to the OPA.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate contract; its termination results in the **Automatic Termination** of the microFIT contract (Clause 8.3).\n*   **Assignment:** The transfer of rights/obligations. Allowed only in total (not partial) to another Eligible Participant, subject to OPA consent.\n*   **Governing Law:** The laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada.\n*   **Arbitration:** A voluntary alternative dispute resolution mechanism if amicable good faith efforts fail after 90 days.\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Technical Terms**\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to a maximum of **10 kW**; modification to increase this is prohibited (Clause 5.1.3).\n*   **Inverter Rating / Solar Array Rating:** Technical specifications from Part 1 that the Supplier is barred from modifying (Clause 5.1.4).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity that must own and operate the Facility’s meter.\n*   **Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** Data required to ensure the facility meets Ontario-sourced equipment requirements.\n*   **Reference Number:** The unique identifier required for all formal e-mail communications with the OPA.\n*   **Generation Payment:** Financial payments for electricity; OPA has the right to audit settlement statements and invoices to verify accuracy." "### Section Headings and Clause Numbers\n*   **[Unnamed Section] (Continuation of Dispute Resolution):** Found on Page 10, covering arbitration procedures and OPA's right to consolidate similar claims.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY:** Outlines OPA guarantees regarding Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES:**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for multi-entity suppliers.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a supplier group.\n*   **APPENDIX A - DEFINITIONS:** Provides legal and technical meanings for specific terms used throughout the contract.\n\n### Key Legal and Financial Terms\n*   **Arbitrator:** An official from the Superior Court of Justice (Toronto Region) empowered under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)* to deliver final and binding decisions.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** A legal obligation where all parties in a group are collectively and individually responsible for the entire liability or obligation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments guaranteed by the OPA if the Local Distribution Company (LDC) fails to pay under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Abut:** Specifically defined property boundaries sharing a common border or separated by a right-of-way of 15 metres or less.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal definition used to group land parcels based on Property Identification Numbers (PINs) or ownership for program eligibility.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and interests (credits, offsets, certificates) associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and initial payment to the supplier.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The central counterparty to the contract.\n*   **Retail Settlement Code / Distribution System Code:** Regulatory frameworks established by the Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** The financial index used for potential price adjustments, established by Statistics Canada.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the standard arbitration prerequisite." "### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Definitions (Unlabeled Section, Pages 14-15):** Includes definitions from \"LDC\" through \"Term.\"\n*   **APPENDIX B: CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE (Page 16):**\n    *   Clauses (a) and (b) regarding Indexed Pricing Periods.\n*   **APPENDIX C: SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE (Pages 17-18):**\n    *   **ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS:** Definitions for \"Existing Building\" and \"Rooftop Facility.\"\n    *   **DOMESTIC CONTENT REQUIREMENTS:** Clauses 1.1 through 1.7.\n    *   **Table 1:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Crystalline Silicon PV Technology.\n    *   **Table 2:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Thin-Film PV Technology.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **Financial/Pricing Terms:**\n    *   **Contract Price:** The base price for electricity.\n    *   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price based on CPI.\n    *   **Percentage Escalated (PE):** The portion of the price subject to inflation adjustments.\n    *   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Used for calculating price escalation.\n    *   **Settlement Price/Settlement Period:** Terms governing the payment and accounting for electricity sales.\n*   **Technical/Regulatory Terms:**\n    *   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to 10 kW for microFIT eligibility.\n    *   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including location (Ontario), fuel type, and connection to the IESO Controlled Grid.\n    *   **Domestic Content Level/Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** The percentage of equipment/services that must originate in Ontario.\n    *   **Designated Activities:** Specific manufacturing or service tasks that earn \"Qualifying Percentages\" toward domestic content targets.\n    *   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, and waterpower.\n    *   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for local electricity delivery.\n    *   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Regulatory permit from the Ministry of the Environment.\n    *   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Zoning/legal status of the property (Residential, Agricultural, Commercial, Industrial).\n    *   **Property Identification Number (PIN):** Legal identifier for land parcels." "### **Legal and Financial Analysis: microFIT Version 2.0 (Page 19-23)**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Table 3: Domestic Content Grid** – Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Concentrated PV Technology.\n*   **APPENDIX D -1: DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clause 1.1)\n    *   Clause 2: Covenants (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **APPENDIX D -2: INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Permitted Battery Back-up Configuration\n*   **APPENDIX E: LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   Clause 3: Additional Terms and Conditions (Sub-clauses 3.1 through 3.6)\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Explicit assertions made by the Supplier (e.g., regarding battery backup and distributor status) upon which the OPA (Ontario Power Authority) relies to enter the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises the Supplier must fulfill throughout the Term of the contract.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** A broad definition including federal/provincial statutes, IESO Market Rules, and OEB (Ontario Energy Board) codes.\n*   **Force Majeure/Disconnection:** Provision 3.3 defines a \"deemed permanent disconnection\" if a facility is offline for more than 20 continuous Business Days.\n*   **Information Rights/Access:** The OPA is granted irrevocable authorization to access meter data and third-party information (Clauses 3.4, 3.5).\n*   **Resident in Ontario:** A qualifying criterion for labor and services to meet domestic content requirements.\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Operational Terms**\n*   **Designated Activity / Qualifying Percentage:** These define the \"Domestic Content\" requirements. For Concentrated PV, items like cells (14%), primary optics (9%), and labor (19%) contribute to a mandatory 100% total.\n*   **Ontario Supplier:** A vendor required for qualifying electrical hardware (5%–9% toward domestic content).\n*   **Generation Payments:** Financial settlements for power produced, specifically handled through the IESO for LDC Suppliers (Clause 3.2).\n*   **In Parallel:** A specific technical/metering configuration defining the relationship between the facility, the load customer, and the distribution system.\n\n#### **4. Referenced Regulatory Bodies/Codes**\n*   **OPA:** Ontario Power Authority.\n*   **IESO:** Independent Electricity System Operator.\n*   **OEB:** Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **Applicable Codes:** Electricity Act 1998, Transmission System Code, Distribution System Code, Retail Settlement Code."]}, :v3_full_map {:summary ["### **Section Headings and Clauses**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. CONTRACT AND SUPPLIER INFORMATION**\n    *   (1) Reference Number\n    *   (2) Supplier Name\n    *   (3) Contract Commencement Date\n    *   (4) Contract End Date\n    *   (5) Legal Entity Relationship to LDC (Connection Agreement)\n    *   (6) LDC Generator Account Number\n    *   (7) Contract Price\n    *   (8) Percentage Escalated\n    *   (9) Base Date\n    *   (10) Supplier Contact Information\n    *   (11) Representative Contact Information\n*   **B. FACILITY CHARACTERISTICS**\n    *   (1) LDC Distribution System Connection\n    *   (2) Facility Location (PIN and Address)\n    *   (3) Renewable Fuel type\n    *   (4) Nameplate Capacity (kW)\n    *   (5) Solar PV Specifics (Inverter/Array ratings, Rooftop status)\n    *   (6) Connection type (Directly/Indirectly/In Parallel)\n    *   (7) Battery Back-up compliance\n    *   (8) Wind Capacity specifics\n*   **C. DOCUMENTS INCLUDED; DEFINED TERMS**\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. TERM**\n*   **2. PRICING PROVISIONS AND PAYMENT**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price\n    *   2.2. Payment (Generation Payments, Settlement Period)\n*   **3. ENVIRONMENTAL ATTRIBUTES**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register (Regulatory Environmental Attributes)\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES**\n    *   4.1. Connection\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics\n    *   4.3. Metering\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility\n*   **5. COVENANTS**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for distribution and payment.\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kWh.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The rate adjusted for inflation/escalation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made to the supplier for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.).\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and credits associated with renewable energy production.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kW.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A supplier meeting specific program requirements.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit for facility operations.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements including the *Electricity Act, 1998*.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legally binding assertions regarding the facility and supplier status.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises to maintain facility characteristics and notify of changes." "### **Project Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **Section 5: [Continued from previous]**\n    *   **5.1.3**: Restrictions on increasing Nameplate Capacity (Max 10 kW).\n    *   **5.1.4**: Restrictions on modifying solar PV inverter/array ratings or facility character.\n*   **5.2: Metering**\n    *   **5.2.1**: Exclusivity of the meter to the Facility.\n    *   **5.2.2**: Ownership/operation of the meter by the Local Distribution Company (LDC).\n*   **5.3: Eligibility**\n    *   **5.3.1**: Requirement to maintain status as an \"Eligible Participant.\"\n*   **Section 6: GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1**: Access Rights (Inspection and Audit).\n    *   **6.2**: Electricity (Prohibition of substituted electricity sources).\n    *   **6.3**: Meter and Meter Data (Access and data release authorization).\n    *   **6.4**: Freedom of Information (FIPPA compliance).\n    *   **6.5**: Collection, Disclosure, and Consent of Information.\n    *   **6.6**: Statement Copies (Document production and verification).\n    *   **6.7**: Supplier Verification and Use of a Representative.\n*   **Section 7: NOTICES**\n    *   **7.1**: Address for Notice (OPA and Supplier email protocols).\n    *   **7.2**: Change of Contact Information (Prescribed Form requirement).\n    *   **7.3**: Timing of Notice (Deemed receipt rules).\n*   **Section 8: TERMINATION**\n    *   **8.1**: Termination on Notice (30 days by Supplier).\n    *   **8.2**: Termination for Breach (10 Business Days cure period).\n    *   **8.3**: Automatic Termination (Upon termination of Connection Agreement).\n*   **Section 9: AMENDMENT** (Requirement for written agreement in Prescribed Form).\n*   **Section 10: ASSIGNMENT** (Conditions for transferring rights).\n*   **Section 11: GOVERNING LAW** (Ontario and Canadian federal laws).\n*   **Section 12: DISPUTE RESOLUTION** (Good faith efforts and Arbitration).\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The maximum rated output of the facility (capped at 10 kW).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity owning the meter and managing local grid connection.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain to remain in the program.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The contracting authority (and its successors).\n*   **FIPPA:** *Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act*.\n*   **Prescribed Form:** Specific templates or formats required by the OPA for formal notifications/amendments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate required contract for grid synchronization; its termination triggers automatic contract termination.\n*   **Assignment:** The legal transfer of contract rights/obligations to a third party.\n*   **Arbitration:** The defined process for resolving disputes outside of court via an Arbitrator.\n*   **Business Day:** Defined for the purpose of identifying notice deadlines (cutoff 5:00 p.m.)." "This section of the **microFIT Version 3.1.1** contract details dispute resolution mechanisms, payment guarantees, liability for multi-party suppliers, and the commencement of the definitions appendix.\n\n### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **[No Heading] (Dispute Resolution Continued)**\n    *   Unnumbered clauses addressing Arbitrator powers under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*, finality of decisions, and OPA’s right to consolidate similar supplier claims for efficiency.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY**\n    *   Addresses OPA’s guarantee of Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for suppliers not acting as a single legal entity.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a multi-person supplier.\n*   **APPENDIX A: DEFINITIONS**\n    *   Alphabetical list of defined terms used throughout the agreement.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal / Procedural Terms:**\n*   **Arbitration:** Process governed by the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*; seat is Toronto.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** Legal obligation where all parties in a group are individually and collectively responsible for the entire liability.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the prerequisite dispute resolution process.\n*   **Abut:** Technical definition regarding property boundaries and rights-of-way.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal classification based on Property Identification Numbers, the *Planning Act (Ontario)*, or Crown/Reserve land status.\n*   **Governmental Authority:** Includes federal, provincial, or municipal bodies (e.g., Ontario Energy Board, Electrical Safety Authority).\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, bylaws, common law, and the Retail Settlement Code.\n\n**Financial / Technical Terms:**\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The primary contracting party and guarantor.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for making payments to the supplier in the first instance.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments payable to the Supplier under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Contract Price:** The per kWh price determined by the **FIT Price Schedule** and the **Base Date**.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Ontario-specific index used for economic adjustments.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights to renewable energy certificates, carbon offsets, and emission reduction allowances.\n*   **Directly vs. Indirectly Connected Facility:** Classification based on whether the facility's connection is independent of or associated with a load customer." "### **Section Headings and Annexes**\n*   **Appendix A (Continued):** (Concluding definitions from the previous section).\n*   **Appendix B:** CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE.\n*   **Appendix C:** SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-1:** DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-2:** INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix E:** LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE.\n\n### **Clause Numbers**\n*   **Appendix D-1:**\n    *   1. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clause 1.1)\n    *   2. COVENANTS (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **Appendix D-2:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. PERMITTED BATTERY BACK-UP CONFIGURATION\n*   **Appendix E:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   3. ADDITIONAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS (Clauses 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The electricity distributor named in the contract.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The rated capacity of the facility (max 10 kW).\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the Contract Price subject to CPI-based increases.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including renewable fuel type, Ontario location, and metering standards.\n*   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, or waterpower.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price (CPy):** The price adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI).\n*   **Rooftop Facility:** A solar project integrated into an existing building structure.\n*   **In Parallel:** A metering configuration where the facility is between the load customer and the distribution system.\n*   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Legal status of land use (e.g., residential vs. agricultural).\n*   **IESO (Independent Electricity System Operator):** The entity governing the Ontario electricity market.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, by-laws, IESO market rules, and OEB codes.\n*   **Commercial Operation:** The milestone marking the official start of energy production for the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations for the Supplier, particularly regarding battery configurations and connection types." "**Sections and Clause Numbers:**\n*   **3.5**: Data release and third-party authorization requirements.\n*   **3.6**: Records retention, settlement statements, and exclusion of General Terms and Conditions.\n\n**Key Legal and Financial Terms:**\n*   **Advanced Notice**: A requirement for the OPA to provide at least two days' notice for meter access.\n*   **Irrevocably Authorize**: A legal requirement for the Supplier to give permanent permission to third parties/agencies to share data with the OPA.\n*   **Administering the Contract**: The defined purpose for which data and information may be requested or shared.\n*   **Settlement Statements**: Financial documents detailing the calculation of payments for electricity generated.\n*   **Generation Payment**: The financial compensation paid to the Supplier for electricity produced by the Facility.\n*   **Section 6.6 of Part 2**: A specific provision of the general contract terms that is explicitly declared not to apply to this agreement."]}}, :node-id #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225", :event/id #uuid "019e4327-5479-702d-b4f2-fe43c9220df3"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xxu1xJ-gxmnzNU1owhfFAOkOX", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111546, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xxu1xJ-gxmnzNU1owhfFAOkOX", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xy8crbr5DQGf81TeA0nEBgd2p", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xy8crbr5DQGf81TeA0nEBgd2p", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi2EMGIyK5fY2KH_jy_v3to6aKp3", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111547, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 1153334, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717", :event/tags #{[:sheet #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225"] [:tick #uuid "219b2581-94f2-4a59-a930-d4b10b8a2717"] [:node #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:11:51.545818-05:00", :inputs {:v2_full_map {:summary ["### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. Contract and Supplier Information**: Clauses (1) through (11).\n*   **B. Facility Characteristics**: Clauses (1) through (8).\n*   **C. Documents Included; Defined Terms**: Unnumbered list of Appendices (A through E).\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. Term**\n*   **2. Pricing Provisions and Payment**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price (2.1.1, 2.1.2)\n    *   2.2. Payment (2.2.1, 2.2.2)\n*   **3. Environmental Attributes**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. Representations and Warranties**\n    *   4.1. Connection (4.1.1–4.1.3)\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics (4.2.1–4.2.3)\n    *   4.3. Metering (4.3.1–4.3.3)\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance (4.4.1–4.4.6)\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility (4.5.1–4.5.3)\n*   **5. Covenants**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics (5.1.1)\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal Terms**\n*   **Ontario Power Authority (OPA):** The contracting entity/procurer.\n*   **Supplier:** The legal entity/individual constructing and operating the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and payments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** The Micro-Embedded Generation Facility Connection Agreement.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements the Supplier must follow.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights, titles, and interests associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **Regulatory Environmental Attributes:** Attributes created/allocated under Laws and Regulations.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit (if applicable).\n*   **Eligible Participant:** Specific status required for Supplier eligibility as defined in the rules.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legal assurances provided by the Supplier to the OPA regarding facts and compliance.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises made by the Supplier for the duration of the contract term.\n\n**Financial Terms**\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kilowatt-hour ($/kWh).\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price taking into account escalation factors.\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the price subject to indexation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made by the LDC for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The periodic billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.) for payments.\n*   **Base Date:** The reference date used for price calculations.\n*   **Domestic Content Level:** Requirement for a minimum percentage (60% for solar PV) of local sourcing for equipment.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kilowatts (kW)." "### **Legal and Financial Summary: microFIT Contract Version 2.0**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **5.1. (Continued):** Specific Covenants (Clauses 5.1.2 – 5.1.4)\n*   **5.2. Metering:** (Clauses 5.2.1 – 5.2.2)\n*   **5.3. Eligibility:** (Clause 5.3.1)\n*   **6. GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1. Access Rights**\n    *   **6.2. Electricity**\n    *   **6.3. Meter and Meter Data:** (Clauses 6.3.1 – 6.3.2)\n    *   **6.4. Freedom of Information**\n    *   **6.5. Collection of Information** (Includes sub-headers: *Disclosure of Information* and *Consent*)\n    *   **6.6. Statement Copies**\n    *   **6.7. Supplier Verification and use of a Representative**\n*   **7. NOTICES:** (Clauses 7.1 – 7.3)\n*   **8. TERMINATION:** (Clauses 8.1 – 8.3)\n*   **9. AMENDMENT**\n*   **10. ASSIGNMENT**\n*   **11. GOVERNING LAW**\n*   **12. DISPUTE RESOLUTION**\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain \"at all times\" to remain in the program.\n*   **FIPPA (Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act):** Acknowledges that the OPA is subject to public disclosure laws regarding the data held.\n*   **Irrevocable Authorization:** The Supplier’s permanent grant of permission to the LDC to release facility data to the OPA.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate contract; its termination results in the **Automatic Termination** of the microFIT contract (Clause 8.3).\n*   **Assignment:** The transfer of rights/obligations. Allowed only in total (not partial) to another Eligible Participant, subject to OPA consent.\n*   **Governing Law:** The laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada.\n*   **Arbitration:** A voluntary alternative dispute resolution mechanism if amicable good faith efforts fail after 90 days.\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Technical Terms**\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to a maximum of **10 kW**; modification to increase this is prohibited (Clause 5.1.3).\n*   **Inverter Rating / Solar Array Rating:** Technical specifications from Part 1 that the Supplier is barred from modifying (Clause 5.1.4).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity that must own and operate the Facility’s meter.\n*   **Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** Data required to ensure the facility meets Ontario-sourced equipment requirements.\n*   **Reference Number:** The unique identifier required for all formal e-mail communications with the OPA.\n*   **Generation Payment:** Financial payments for electricity; OPA has the right to audit settlement statements and invoices to verify accuracy." "### Section Headings and Clause Numbers\n*   **[Unnamed Section] (Continuation of Dispute Resolution):** Found on Page 10, covering arbitration procedures and OPA's right to consolidate similar claims.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY:** Outlines OPA guarantees regarding Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES:**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for multi-entity suppliers.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a supplier group.\n*   **APPENDIX A - DEFINITIONS:** Provides legal and technical meanings for specific terms used throughout the contract.\n\n### Key Legal and Financial Terms\n*   **Arbitrator:** An official from the Superior Court of Justice (Toronto Region) empowered under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)* to deliver final and binding decisions.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** A legal obligation where all parties in a group are collectively and individually responsible for the entire liability or obligation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments guaranteed by the OPA if the Local Distribution Company (LDC) fails to pay under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Abut:** Specifically defined property boundaries sharing a common border or separated by a right-of-way of 15 metres or less.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal definition used to group land parcels based on Property Identification Numbers (PINs) or ownership for program eligibility.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and interests (credits, offsets, certificates) associated with the environmental benefits of the facility.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for the distribution system and initial payment to the supplier.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The central counterparty to the contract.\n*   **Retail Settlement Code / Distribution System Code:** Regulatory frameworks established by the Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** The financial index used for potential price adjustments, established by Statistics Canada.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the standard arbitration prerequisite." "### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Definitions (Unlabeled Section, Pages 14-15):** Includes definitions from \"LDC\" through \"Term.\"\n*   **APPENDIX B: CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE (Page 16):**\n    *   Clauses (a) and (b) regarding Indexed Pricing Periods.\n*   **APPENDIX C: SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE (Pages 17-18):**\n    *   **ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS:** Definitions for \"Existing Building\" and \"Rooftop Facility.\"\n    *   **DOMESTIC CONTENT REQUIREMENTS:** Clauses 1.1 through 1.7.\n    *   **Table 1:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Crystalline Silicon PV Technology.\n    *   **Table 2:** Domestic Content Grid for Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Thin-Film PV Technology.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **Financial/Pricing Terms:**\n    *   **Contract Price:** The base price for electricity.\n    *   **Indexed Contract Price:** The adjusted price based on CPI.\n    *   **Percentage Escalated (PE):** The portion of the price subject to inflation adjustments.\n    *   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Used for calculating price escalation.\n    *   **Settlement Price/Settlement Period:** Terms governing the payment and accounting for electricity sales.\n*   **Technical/Regulatory Terms:**\n    *   **Nameplate Capacity:** Limited to 10 kW for microFIT eligibility.\n    *   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including location (Ontario), fuel type, and connection to the IESO Controlled Grid.\n    *   **Domestic Content Level/Minimum Required Domestic Content Level:** The percentage of equipment/services that must originate in Ontario.\n    *   **Designated Activities:** Specific manufacturing or service tasks that earn \"Qualifying Percentages\" toward domestic content targets.\n    *   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, and waterpower.\n    *   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for local electricity delivery.\n    *   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Regulatory permit from the Ministry of the Environment.\n    *   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Zoning/legal status of the property (Residential, Agricultural, Commercial, Industrial).\n    *   **Property Identification Number (PIN):** Legal identifier for land parcels." "### **Legal and Financial Analysis: microFIT Version 2.0 (Page 19-23)**\n\n#### **1. Section Headings and Clause Numbers**\n*   **Table 3: Domestic Content Grid** – Micro-Scale (≤10kW) Solar Photovoltaic Power Projects Utilizing Concentrated PV Technology.\n*   **APPENDIX D -1: DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clause 1.1)\n    *   Clause 2: Covenants (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **APPENDIX D -2: INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Permitted Battery Back-up Configuration\n*   **APPENDIX E: LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE**\n    *   Clause 1: Additional Defined Terms\n    *   Clause 2: Representations and Warranties (Sub-clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   Clause 3: Additional Terms and Conditions (Sub-clauses 3.1 through 3.6)\n\n#### **2. Key Legal Terms**\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Explicit assertions made by the Supplier (e.g., regarding battery backup and distributor status) upon which the OPA (Ontario Power Authority) relies to enter the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises the Supplier must fulfill throughout the Term of the contract.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** A broad definition including federal/provincial statutes, IESO Market Rules, and OEB (Ontario Energy Board) codes.\n*   **Force Majeure/Disconnection:** Provision 3.3 defines a \"deemed permanent disconnection\" if a facility is offline for more than 20 continuous Business Days.\n*   **Information Rights/Access:** The OPA is granted irrevocable authorization to access meter data and third-party information (Clauses 3.4, 3.5).\n*   **Resident in Ontario:** A qualifying criterion for labor and services to meet domestic content requirements.\n\n#### **3. Key Financial & Operational Terms**\n*   **Designated Activity / Qualifying Percentage:** These define the \"Domestic Content\" requirements. For Concentrated PV, items like cells (14%), primary optics (9%), and labor (19%) contribute to a mandatory 100% total.\n*   **Ontario Supplier:** A vendor required for qualifying electrical hardware (5%–9% toward domestic content).\n*   **Generation Payments:** Financial settlements for power produced, specifically handled through the IESO for LDC Suppliers (Clause 3.2).\n*   **In Parallel:** A specific technical/metering configuration defining the relationship between the facility, the load customer, and the distribution system.\n\n#### **4. Referenced Regulatory Bodies/Codes**\n*   **OPA:** Ontario Power Authority.\n*   **IESO:** Independent Electricity System Operator.\n*   **OEB:** Ontario Energy Board.\n*   **Applicable Codes:** Electricity Act 1998, Transmission System Code, Distribution System Code, Retail Settlement Code."]}, :v3_full_map {:summary ["### **Section Headings and Clauses**\n\n**Part 1 – Contract Details**\n*   **A. CONTRACT AND SUPPLIER INFORMATION**\n    *   (1) Reference Number\n    *   (2) Supplier Name\n    *   (3) Contract Commencement Date\n    *   (4) Contract End Date\n    *   (5) Legal Entity Relationship to LDC (Connection Agreement)\n    *   (6) LDC Generator Account Number\n    *   (7) Contract Price\n    *   (8) Percentage Escalated\n    *   (9) Base Date\n    *   (10) Supplier Contact Information\n    *   (11) Representative Contact Information\n*   **B. FACILITY CHARACTERISTICS**\n    *   (1) LDC Distribution System Connection\n    *   (2) Facility Location (PIN and Address)\n    *   (3) Renewable Fuel type\n    *   (4) Nameplate Capacity (kW)\n    *   (5) Solar PV Specifics (Inverter/Array ratings, Rooftop status)\n    *   (6) Connection type (Directly/Indirectly/In Parallel)\n    *   (7) Battery Back-up compliance\n    *   (8) Wind Capacity specifics\n*   **C. DOCUMENTS INCLUDED; DEFINED TERMS**\n\n**Part 2 – General Terms and Conditions**\n*   **1. TERM**\n*   **2. PRICING PROVISIONS AND PAYMENT**\n    *   2.1. Indexed Contract Price\n    *   2.2. Payment (Generation Payments, Settlement Period)\n*   **3. ENVIRONMENTAL ATTRIBUTES**\n    *   3.1. Transfer\n    *   3.2. Action to Transfer\n    *   3.3. Action to Register (Regulatory Environmental Attributes)\n    *   3.4. Cost Reimbursement\n*   **4. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES**\n    *   4.1. Connection\n    *   4.2. Facility Characteristics\n    *   4.3. Metering\n    *   4.4. Necessary Rights and Compliance\n    *   4.5. Supplier Eligibility\n*   **5. COVENANTS**\n    *   5.1. Facility Characteristics\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for distribution and payment.\n*   **Contract Price:** The base rate per kWh.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price:** The rate adjusted for inflation/escalation.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments made to the supplier for electricity injected into the grid.\n*   **Settlement Period:** The billing cycle (monthly, quarterly, etc.).\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights and credits associated with renewable energy production.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The total designed output of the facility in kW.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A supplier meeting specific program requirements.\n*   **Renewable Energy Approval:** Required regulatory permit for facility operations.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Statutory requirements including the *Electricity Act, 1998*.\n*   **Representations and Warranties:** Legally binding assertions regarding the facility and supplier status.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing promises to maintain facility characteristics and notify of changes." "### **Project Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **Section 5: [Continued from previous]**\n    *   **5.1.3**: Restrictions on increasing Nameplate Capacity (Max 10 kW).\n    *   **5.1.4**: Restrictions on modifying solar PV inverter/array ratings or facility character.\n*   **5.2: Metering**\n    *   **5.2.1**: Exclusivity of the meter to the Facility.\n    *   **5.2.2**: Ownership/operation of the meter by the Local Distribution Company (LDC).\n*   **5.3: Eligibility**\n    *   **5.3.1**: Requirement to maintain status as an \"Eligible Participant.\"\n*   **Section 6: GENERAL CONDITIONS**\n    *   **6.1**: Access Rights (Inspection and Audit).\n    *   **6.2**: Electricity (Prohibition of substituted electricity sources).\n    *   **6.3**: Meter and Meter Data (Access and data release authorization).\n    *   **6.4**: Freedom of Information (FIPPA compliance).\n    *   **6.5**: Collection, Disclosure, and Consent of Information.\n    *   **6.6**: Statement Copies (Document production and verification).\n    *   **6.7**: Supplier Verification and Use of a Representative.\n*   **Section 7: NOTICES**\n    *   **7.1**: Address for Notice (OPA and Supplier email protocols).\n    *   **7.2**: Change of Contact Information (Prescribed Form requirement).\n    *   **7.3**: Timing of Notice (Deemed receipt rules).\n*   **Section 8: TERMINATION**\n    *   **8.1**: Termination on Notice (30 days by Supplier).\n    *   **8.2**: Termination for Breach (10 Business Days cure period).\n    *   **8.3**: Automatic Termination (Upon termination of Connection Agreement).\n*   **Section 9: AMENDMENT** (Requirement for written agreement in Prescribed Form).\n*   **Section 10: ASSIGNMENT** (Conditions for transferring rights).\n*   **Section 11: GOVERNING LAW** (Ontario and Canadian federal laws).\n*   **Section 12: DISPUTE RESOLUTION** (Good faith efforts and Arbitration).\n\n---\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The maximum rated output of the facility (capped at 10 kW).\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity owning the meter and managing local grid connection.\n*   **Eligible Participant:** A status the Supplier must maintain to remain in the program.\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The contracting authority (and its successors).\n*   **FIPPA:** *Ontario Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act*.\n*   **Prescribed Form:** Specific templates or formats required by the OPA for formal notifications/amendments.\n*   **Connection Agreement:** A separate required contract for grid synchronization; its termination triggers automatic contract termination.\n*   **Assignment:** The legal transfer of contract rights/obligations to a third party.\n*   **Arbitration:** The defined process for resolving disputes outside of court via an Arbitrator.\n*   **Business Day:** Defined for the purpose of identifying notice deadlines (cutoff 5:00 p.m.)." "This section of the **microFIT Version 3.1.1** contract details dispute resolution mechanisms, payment guarantees, liability for multi-party suppliers, and the commencement of the definitions appendix.\n\n### **Sections and Clause Numbers**\n\n*   **[No Heading] (Dispute Resolution Continued)**\n    *   Unnumbered clauses addressing Arbitrator powers under the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*, finality of decisions, and OPA’s right to consolidate similar supplier claims for efficiency.\n*   **13. LDC FAILURE TO PAY**\n    *   Addresses OPA’s guarantee of Generation Payments.\n*   **14. SUPPLIERS COMPOSED OF MULTIPLE ENTITIES**\n    *   **14.1. Joint and Several Liability:** Defines liability for suppliers not acting as a single legal entity.\n    *   **14.2. Removal of Person forming Supplier:** Procedures for changing the composition of a multi-person supplier.\n*   **APPENDIX A: DEFINITIONS**\n    *   Alphabetical list of defined terms used throughout the agreement.\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n\n**Legal / Procedural Terms:**\n*   **Arbitration:** Process governed by the *Arbitrations Act, 1991 (Ontario)*; seat is Toronto.\n*   **Joint and Several Liability:** Legal obligation where all parties in a group are individually and collectively responsible for the entire liability.\n*   **Injunctive or Declaratory Relief:** Legal remedies exempt from the prerequisite dispute resolution process.\n*   **Abut:** Technical definition regarding property boundaries and rights-of-way.\n*   **Deemed Single Property:** A legal classification based on Property Identification Numbers, the *Planning Act (Ontario)*, or Crown/Reserve land status.\n*   **Governmental Authority:** Includes federal, provincial, or municipal bodies (e.g., Ontario Energy Board, Electrical Safety Authority).\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, bylaws, common law, and the Retail Settlement Code.\n\n**Financial / Technical Terms:**\n*   **OPA (Ontario Power Authority):** The primary contracting party and guarantor.\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The entity responsible for making payments to the supplier in the first instance.\n*   **Generation Payments:** Payments payable to the Supplier under the Connection Agreement.\n*   **Contract Price:** The per kWh price determined by the **FIT Price Schedule** and the **Base Date**.\n*   **CPI (Consumer Price Index):** Ontario-specific index used for economic adjustments.\n*   **Environmental Attributes:** Rights to renewable energy certificates, carbon offsets, and emission reduction allowances.\n*   **Directly vs. Indirectly Connected Facility:** Classification based on whether the facility's connection is independent of or associated with a load customer." "### **Section Headings and Annexes**\n*   **Appendix A (Continued):** (Concluding definitions from the previous section).\n*   **Appendix B:** CALCULATION OF INDEXED CONTRACT PRICE.\n*   **Appendix C:** SOLAR PHOTOVOLTAIC SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-1:** DIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix D-2:** INDIRECTLY CONNECTED FACILITY SCHEDULE.\n*   **Appendix E:** LDC SUPPLIER SCHEDULE.\n\n### **Clause Numbers**\n*   **Appendix D-1:**\n    *   1. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clause 1.1)\n    *   2. COVENANTS (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n*   **Appendix D-2:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. PERMITTED BATTERY BACK-UP CONFIGURATION\n*   **Appendix E:**\n    *   1. ADDITIONAL DEFINED TERMS\n    *   2. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES (Clauses 2.1, 2.2)\n    *   3. ADDITIONAL TERMS AND CONDITIONS (Clauses 3.1, 3.2, 3.3, 3.4)\n\n### **Key Legal and Financial Terms**\n*   **LDC (Local Distribution Company):** The electricity distributor named in the contract.\n*   **Nameplate Capacity:** The rated capacity of the facility (max 10 kW).\n*   **Percentage Escalated:** The portion of the Contract Price subject to CPI-based increases.\n*   **Project Eligibility Requirements:** Criteria including renewable fuel type, Ontario location, and metering standards.\n*   **Renewable Fuel:** Defined sources including wind, solar (PV), Renewable Biomass, Biogas, landfill gas, or waterpower.\n*   **Indexed Contract Price (CPy):** The price adjusted annually based on the Consumer Price Index (CPI).\n*   **Rooftop Facility:** A solar project integrated into an existing building structure.\n*   **In Parallel:** A metering configuration where the facility is between the load customer and the distribution system.\n*   **Lawfully Permitted Use:** Legal status of land use (e.g., residential vs. agricultural).\n*   **IESO (Independent Electricity System Operator):** The entity governing the Ontario electricity market.\n*   **Laws and Regulations:** Broadly defined to include statutes, by-laws, IESO market rules, and OEB codes.\n*   **Commercial Operation:** The milestone marking the official start of energy production for the contract.\n*   **Covenants:** Ongoing obligations for the Supplier, particularly regarding battery configurations and connection types." "**Sections and Clause Numbers:**\n*   **3.5**: Data release and third-party authorization requirements.\n*   **3.6**: Records retention, settlement statements, and exclusion of General Terms and Conditions.\n\n**Key Legal and Financial Terms:**\n*   **Advanced Notice**: A requirement for the OPA to provide at least two days' notice for meter access.\n*   **Irrevocably Authorize**: A legal requirement for the Supplier to give permanent permission to third parties/agencies to share data with the OPA.\n*   **Administering the Contract**: The defined purpose for which data and information may be requested or shared.\n*   **Settlement Statements**: Financial documents detailing the calculation of payments for electricity generated.\n*   **Generation Payment**: The financial compensation paid to the Supplier for electricity produced by the Facility.\n*   **Section 6.6 of Part 2**: A specific provision of the general contract terms that is explicitly declared not to apply to this agreement."]}}, :node-id #uuid "048aeda4-e8e7-49f2-86b6-37208d7129c8", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "b5bd8208-dee2-409f-b862-7761ff30e225", :event/id #uuid "019e4327-5479-702d-b4f2-fe43c9220df3"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xy8crbr5DQGf81TeA0nEBgd2p", :mulog/timestamp 1779243111546, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3ZAi1xy8crbr5DQGf81TeA0nEBgd2p", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
